    "title": "Volunteers team up to make Wheatland beautiful... - NewsBreak",
    "text": "pcrecordtimes.com\nwebsite\nWheatland\nVolunteers team up to make Wheatland beautiful...\nBy Record-Times welcomes Murr to editorial staff,\n22 hours agoAfter a hot, dry summer the volunteers responsible for the beautiful flower beds on the west side of 16th Street from the Chamber of Commerce to the stoplight are winding up their hard work. There are eleven beds cared for by: Barbara and Ron Stugart, Shelley Marker (Holy Sprouts), Joanie McKee, Kelly Atterbury, Dan Brecht, Diane Schroeder, Jana Bjelkevig, Platte Valley Bank (two beds), Colleen Holtzclaw and Donna Dannemiller. Also pictured are Mike Lambert and Jason Niemi, Wheatland City employees who work with us semi-constantly it seems, to keep the drip systems to the flower beds working properly. Ruth Moyte, owner of Red Dandelion, donated her services to create the colorful signs on each bed thanking the individual volunteers. Many years ago, before the present landscaping was done, Ruth’s late father, Bob Noyce, could be seen mowing this entire area with his old tractor as a volunteer. Ruth sees her donation as a way to honor her father.\n2",
